  data: {
    LLM: "Don't get attached to your hand until the 6th card is dealt. A pair of Aces is great, but if 9s suddenly become wild on the 6th street, you might be instantly losing to a Three-of-a-Kind.\n\nThe 'Queen Hunt': If you are looking for a specific rank to fill a Straight, hoping for a Queen to appear can be a viable strategy, as it effectively doubles your 'outs'.\n\nPsychology of Shifting Wilds: If the wild card changes late in the hand, players who were betting aggressively on the previous wild card will often go into 'check' mode. Use this hesitation to bluff if you can represent the new wild card.",
    Player: "Don't get attached to your hand until the 6th card is dealt. A pair of Aces is great, but if 9s suddenly become wild on the 6th street, you might be instantly losing to a Three-of-a-Kind.\n\nThe 'Queen Hunt': If you are looking for a specific rank to fill a Straight, hoping for a Queen to appear can be a viable strategy, as it effectively doubles your 'outs'.\n\nPsychology of Shifting Wilds: If the wild card changes late in the hand, players who were betting aggressively on the previous wild card will often go into 'check' mode. Use this hesitation to bluff if you can represent the new wild card.",
